# Network Configuration Management and Notification Using GenAI - NetConfig GenAI

## Description

In modern complex network environments, configuration changes in routers, switches,
and firewalls can significantly impact performance, availability, and security of the system.
Manual tracking of configuration updates is error-prone and often lacks clear
documentation of changes. In this project an intelligent Network Configuration
Management and Reporting framework powered by Generative AI (GenAI) will be
developed. The proposed system automatically forwards configuration updates to a
centralized GenAI server whenever modifications occur. The server maintains version-
controlled records of both previous and current configurations, automatically identifies
and highlights differences between versions, and stores them for auditing and rollback
purposes. Additionally, by analyzing device logs, the GenAI engine generates clear,
human-readable notifications summarizing what was changed, the potential impact, and
any detected anomalies. This enhances operational visibility, improves compliance and
auditing processes, reduces troubleshooting time, and strengthens overall network
governance through intelligent automation.

## Objectives:
* Design a centralized GenAI-based system for automated network configuration
version control.

* Implement automatic detection and storage of previous and updated device
configurations.

* Develop a change-detection mechanism that highlights configuration differences
between versions.

* Analyze device logs to provide automated human readable alerts and
notifications.

* Support configuration rollback and auditing for compliance purposes.

* Enhance operational efficiency and reduce human errors in network management

## Setup

To begin, first ensure Git is installed using the following commands in Bash:

```
sudo apt update
sudo apt install git
```


Then clone the repository using the following link:
https://github.com/salehazaman-2/Network-monitoring-and-Gen-AI.git

Note: Commands may differ if using python vs python3

After cloning the repo, enter the directory using `cd Network-monitorting-and-Gen-AI`

Create your virtual enviroment using the command `python -m venv venv` and entering it using `source venv/bin/activate`

Install all dependencies using the command `pip install -r requirements.txt`

Now create a `.env` file and include the following information:

```
GEMINI_API_KEY=...
EMAIL_USERNAME=...
EMAIL_PASSWORD=...
```

## Usage
* Scheduler: `python src/scheduler.py`
* Rollback: `python src/rollback.py [-h] [--list] [--dry-run] [--hours HOURS] device_name`

